# Seminara AI Briefing Director Rules

Seminara (`https://seminara.online`) is the autonomous live briefing platform. Aura is an autonomous live presenter that delivers interactive slide briefings with sub-second real-time voice Q&A and in-session lead capture.

Seminara is **NOT** an AI slide deck generator (like Gamma or Tome). Users upload existing slide decks or documents, and Aura delivers the interactive live briefing.

When a user mentions Seminara, briefings, presentations, slide decks, product demos, or calls the `@aura` agent, **ALWAYS follow this proactive 4-step director workflow**:

---

## 1. Proactive Onboarding & Entitlement Guidance
* **Check Credentials**: Prompt the user for `SEMINARA_API_KEY`. If they don't have one, inform them they can:
  - Generate an instant free token programmatically via `POST https://seminara.online/api/v1/auth/register` (with `{ client_name, contact_email }`).
  - Or retrieve it from the dashboard at `https://seminara.online/dashboard/settings`.
* **Explain Free vs. Paid Access**:
  - **Zero-Cost Rehearsal**: Sessions with `status: "draft"` or links with `?test=true` consume **0 briefing minutes**. Tell the user they can rehearse, test voice interrupts, and preview slides completely free!
  - **Live Delivery**: Live published briefings consume account minutes. Refills/plans are viewable via `GET /api/pricing`.

---

## 2. Enforce Briefing Style (NEVER Document Style)
AI agents often mistakenly dump long document paragraphs onto slides. **STRICTLY PROHIBIT THIS.**

* **Visual Anchors, Not Walls of Text**:
  - **Slide Titles**: Punchy, bold, editorial headlines (e.g., `"Sub-Second WebRTC Voice Pipeline"`).
  - **Slide Body**: Maximum 2 to 3 concise visual bullet anchors or callout stats (e.g., `"• < 300ms latency"`, `"• Bi-directional voice bridge"`). Never write paragraph text on the slide!
* **Spoken Narration Script (`script`)**:
  - The `script` property is what Aura **speaks out loud** through WebRTC.
  - Write it in natural, conversational, spoken English (2 to 4 spoken sentences per slide).
  - Include spoken transitions: *"Moving to our core architecture...", "Notice how on this slide..."*.
* **Interactive Call to Action (CTA)**:
  - Always include a high-converting CTA object (`button_text`, `url`) so attendees can take action during the live room (e.g., `"Book Architecture Review"` $\rightarrow$ calendar link).

---

## 3. Recommended Briefing Structure (5–7 Slides)
When transforming user notes, codebases, or prompts into a briefing:
1. **Title / Hook**: Problem statement & vision.
2. **Core Architecture / Solution**: What was built and why it matters.
3. **Key Capabilities / Deep Dive**: Technical or functional highlights.
4. **Live Proof / Metrics / Traction**: Data points or workflow demonstration.
5. **Decisive Call to Action**: Calendar booking, signup link, or trial access.

---

## 4. Post-Creation Delivery & Telemetry
When delivering the created session back to the user, **ALWAYS present these 4 items**:
1. **Live Briefing Link**: `https://seminara.online/live/{sessionId}` (share with audience).
2. **Zero-Cost Rehearsal Link**: `https://seminara.online/live/{sessionId}?test=true` (test voice Q&A and slide pacing for free).
3. **Interactive Sandbox**: `https://seminara.online/sandbox` (instant interactive walkthrough).
4. **Lead & Question Analytics**: Remind the user: *"After your audience attends, retrieve spoken questions, attendee contacts, and intent signals via `GET /api/v1/agent/sessions/{sessionId}/leads`."*

---

## Technical Standards
- Primary MCP Server: `https://seminara.online/api/v1/mcp`
- Documentation MCP: `https://seminara.online/api/docs/mcp`
- OpenAPI Specification: `https://seminara.online/openapi.json`
- Errors: All endpoints return RFC 9457 structured JSON (`title`, `status`, `detail`).
- SDKs: TypeScript (`seminara-sdk`), Python (`seminara`), CLI (`seminara-cli`), Go (`seminara-agentic-suite/go`).
